# Titan Arena — Competitive Market Gap Analysis

Benchmarked against **Battlefy**, **Toornament**, **start.gg**, **ESL/FACEIT**, and **Challengermode** to identify every feature gap needed to build a market-beating product.

---

## 🔴 CRITICAL (Breaks core value proposition if absent)

### 1. Real Payment Gateway
| Platform | What they have |
|---|---|
| start.gg | Stripe-powered entry fee collection + instant prize disbursement |
| Toornament | Monetization-first roadmap (2024 priority) |
| **Titan Arena** | ❌ All payment endpoints are [stubHandler](file:///e:/My%20projects/Esports%20Tournament%20Website/CODE/BACKEND/src/modules/wallet/wallet.controller.js#85-89) returning nothing |

**Required**: Integrate Razorpay (India-first) or Stripe. Must support UPI, Netbanking, and Cards. Auto-debit entry fees on registration and auto-credit prizes on tournament completion.

---

### 2. Live Bracket Viewer (Public)
| Platform | What they have |
|---|---|
| start.gg | Interactive public bracket page — anyone can watch live match progression |
| Battlefy | Real-time brackets embedded on the tournament page |
| **Titan Arena** | ❌ No public bracket page exists in the frontend routes |

**Required**: A `/tournaments/:id/bracket` public page built on top of the existing Java Bracket Engine (`GET /api/brackets/{id}`). Should update in real time via WebSocket or polling.

---

### 3. Mobile Responsive Design & PWA
| Platform | What they have |
|---|---|
| ESL FACEIT | Dedicated iOS + Android apps |
| Battlefy | Mobile-optimised web experience |
| **Titan Arena** | ⚠️ Currently desktop-first; no PWA manifest or service worker |

**Required**: Full mobile responsiveness test + PWA (service worker, installable, offline capability). India's mobile-first user base makes this critical.

---

## 🟠 HIGH PRIORITY (Direct conversion drivers)

### 4. Double Elimination & Round Robin Formats
| Platform | What they have |
|---|---|
| start.gg | Single + Double Elimination, Swiss, Round Robin, Custom |
| Challonge | All 5+ formats |
| **Titan Arena** | ⚠️ Java engine supports `SINGLE_ELIMINATION` by default with hooks for others |

**Required**: Enable `DOUBLE_ELIMINATION` and `ROUND_ROBIN` bracket formats in the frontend tournament creation form, and verify the Java BracketController handles the [format](file:///e:/My%20projects/Esports%20Tournament%20Website/CODE/FRONTEND/src/pages/player/TournamentDetailPage.jsx#104-113) parameter correctly.

---

### 5. Clan / Organization System (Schema Ready, UI Missing)
| Platform | What they have |
|---|---|
| Battlefy | Full team + organization management |
| start.gg | Community hubs with recurring events |
| **Titan Arena** | ⚠️ `clan` and `clan_member` tables exist in [schema.js](file:///e:/My%20projects/Esports%20Tournament%20Website/CODE/BACKEND/src/db/schema.js) — ZERO frontend UI |

**Required**: Build `/clans` page with create/join/leave functionality. Allow clans to enter team tournaments as a registered entity.

---

### 6. Achievement & Badge System (Schema Ready, Logic Missing)
| Platform | What they have |
|---|---|
| Battlefy | Game developer achievement validation |
| ESL | Digital badges by achievement tier |
| **Titan Arena** | ⚠️ `achievements` + `user_achievement` tables exist — no award logic or display |

**Required**: Implement automatic achievement unlocking in the Kafka event consumer (e.g., "First Tournament Win", "Win Streak x5"). Display earned badges on the profile page.

---

### 7. Twitch / YouTube Live Stream Integration
| Platform | What they have |
|---|---|
| Battlefy | Direct Twitch broadcast integration per match card |
| start.gg | Stream queue management for live events |
| **Titan Arena** | ⚠️ `streamUrl` field exists in the `match` table — no UI to display or link it |

**Required**: Display the `streamUrl` on the match detail and tournament bracket pages. Add a "Watch Live" button that opens the stream in an embedded player or new tab.

---

### 8. Dispute Resolution UI (Schema Ready, UI Missing)
| Platform | What they have |
|---|---|
| ESL | Formal anti-cheat and match dispute system |
| Battlefy | Admin-mediated dispute resolution |
| **Titan Arena** | ⚠️ `disputes` table with `evidenceUrl`, `resolution`, `status` — no UI anywhere |

**Required**: Add a "Raise Dispute" button on the match result page. Build a Host/Admin panel for reviewing and resolving open disputes.

---

### 9. Match MVP System (Schema Ready, UI Missing)
| Platform | What they have |
|---|---|
| ESL | Post-match MVP highlights |
| **Titan Arena** | ⚠️ `match_mvp` table with MMR bonuses — zero display in the UI |

**Required**: Allow hosts to nominate an MVP after each match. Show MVP badge on the match history card and highlight it on the leaderboard.

---

## 🟡 MEDIUM PRIORITY (Differentiators that win loyalty)

### 10. Team MMR / Ranked Team Queue
Currently only individual `mmr_ratings` are updated. The `team_mmr_rating` table is defined but the Kafka consumer never writes to it.

**Required**: On match completion, also upsert the `team_mmr_rating` table so team-based tournaments can sort players by team Elo, not just individual rating.

---

### 11. Check-In System UI
The `checkins` table and `checkinStart` / `checkinEnd` timestamps exist on the `tournament` table, but no frontend check-in button or countdown exists on [TournamentDetailPage.jsx](file:///e:/My%20projects/Esports%20Tournament%20Website/CODE/FRONTEND/src/pages/player/TournamentDetailPage.jsx).

**Required**: Show a check-in window countdown on the tournament detail page. Players must click "Check In" within the window or get removed from the bracket.

---

### 12. Host Earnings Dashboard (Currently Hardcoded to 0)
[HostUserPayments.jsx](file:///e:/My%20projects/Esports%20Tournament%20Website/CODE/FRONTEND/src/pages/host/HostUserPayments.jsx) has `totalEarnings: 0` with a TODO comment.

**Required**: Query `transactions` table by `tournamentId` for type `HOST_PROFIT` and sum them. Display a proper revenue chart with per-tournament breakdown.

---

### 13. Spectator Code Display
The `spectatorCode` field exists in the `matches` table but is never shown in the frontend match cards.

**Required**: Display the spectator code prominently on the live match card so viewers can join directly in-game.

---

### 14. Player Game Profile Verification
The `playerGameProfiles` table tracks `verificationStatus` (PENDING/VERIFIED), but the admin panel has no UI to verify or reject a submitted in-game profile.

**Required**: Add a "Game ID Verification" section to the Admin Panel listing all `PENDING` entries with approve/reject actions.

---

### 15. KYC / Identity Verification Flow
The `kycRequests` table (with `documentType`, `proofUrl`, `selfieUrl`) exists. The backend `kyc` module folder exists. But no frontend KYC upload page is wired in the player settings.

**Required**: Add a `/settings/kyc` page that collects an ID document + selfie upload (Cloudinary/S3), required for prize withdrawals over a threshold (e.g., ₹10,000).

---

## 🟢 ENHANCEMENTS (Polish that beats competitors on feel)

### 16. In-Game Social Feed (Posts → Tournaments)
[FeedPage.jsx](file:///e:/My%20projects/Esports%20Tournament%20Website/CODE/FRONTEND/src/pages/player/FeedPage.jsx) and `posts` table exist. But posts don't link to tournaments or match events. Competitors use feeds to drive re-engagement.

**Required**: Allow tournament-specific posts ("just won Round 2 of BGMI Pro! 🏆"). Auto-generate achievement posts when a player unlocks a badge.

---

### 17. Notifications (Schema Exists, Push Missing)
The `notifications` table is populated, but there's no push notification backend (FCM / Web Push).

**Required**: Add Firebase Cloud Messaging for browser push notifications. Alert players: "Your match starts in 30 minutes."

---

### 18. Anti-Smurf & Multi-Account Prevention
No system exists to detect duplicate accounts sharing the same in-game ID (`platformUid`).

**Required**: On registration, validate `platformUid` uniqueness. Flag accounts registering from the same IP or device fingerprint.

---

### 19. Tournament Prize Pool Breakdown (On Detail Page)
The `payouts` table supports position-based prize tiers. This is partially rendered in [TournamentDetailPage.jsx](file:///e:/My%20projects/Esports%20Tournament%20Website/CODE/FRONTEND/src/pages/player/TournamentDetailPage.jsx), but the payout records come from the hardcoded mock data, not the database.

**Required**: Fetch `payouts` by `tournamentId` from the backend and display them — not the mock array.

---

### 20. Platform Analytics Dashboard
Competitors publish public stats: total players, prize money distributed, tournaments completed. Titan Arena's admin panel has basic counts but no graphical analytics.

**Required**: Build a time-series chart on the Admin Panel showing user growth, tournament activity, and platform revenue over time using Chart.js or Recharts.

---

